    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the frai CLI. The issue was in how the `gate` command was handling arguments.\n\n### The Problem\nThe original code used `[args...]` as a variadic positional argument, which only captures positional arguments and not flags. Since `--ci` is a flag, it wasn't being included in the `args` array passed to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n### The Solution  \nI modified the gate command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Changed the command definition from `'gate [args...]'` to just `'gate'`\n2. Used `process.argv` directly to extract all arguments after the `gate` command, which includes both positional arguments and flags\n3. Pass all these arguments to the frai-gate CLI\n\n### Verification\nThe fix has been tested and confirmed working:\n- Running `node packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713",
